cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Auren in research, teaching, or a language survey, cite this repository."
title: "Auren: a gradual-typing language with an interpreter and a native C11 backend"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Auren contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zeiad6/auren"
abstract: >-
  Auren is a pre-1.0 programming language with Python-like syntax, optional
  type annotations, a tree-walking reference interpreter, and a native GNU C11
  backend for a statically typed subset. The interpreter is the semantic
  oracle; native behavior is checked by differential tests.
keywords:
  - programming language
  - gradual typing
  - interpreter
  - compiler
  - C11
  - Rust
